  "confidence_interval_audit": {
    "status": "AUDITED_AND_VERIFIED",
    "explanation_of_zero_width_cluster_bootstrap": "Cluster bootstrap resamples canonical groups from the empirical distribution with replacement. When zero false positives exist in the sample (as at tau=0.70), every resampled cluster has 0 false positives, causing the empirical bootstrap distribution of FPR to collapse to a degenerate point mass at 0.0 ([0%, 0%]). This is a known mathematical property of non-parametric bootstrap on zero-count events and cannot be interpreted as proof of zero population error.",
